Noctalia v5.5.0 for Slackware -current (x86_64)
===============================================

What it is
----------
Noctalia is a native Wayland desktop shell (bars, dock, launcher, control
center, notifications, wallpaper, lock screen, session actions, clipboard
history, OSDs, tray). It is built directly on Wayland + OpenGL ES with no Qt
or GTK dependency.

Upstream: https://github.com/noctalia-dev/noctalia
License: MIT (see LICENSE)
Build system: Meson + Ninja; C++23 (needs GCC 13+, system has 16.2)

Runtime deps (all installed on this system)
-------------------------------------------
wayland, wayland-protocols, libepoxy, freetype2, fontconfig, cairo, pango,
harfbuzz, libxkbcommon, glib2, libsecret, libsodium, libpipewire,
wireplumber 0.5, polkit (agent+gobject), libcurl, libwebp, libjxl,
libsndfile, librsvg, libqalculate, libxml2, nlohmann-json, tomlplusplus,
libical, jemalloc, libpam.

Non-core (SBo / built here) dependencies:
  * sdbus-cpp   - high-level C++ D-Bus library (built in libraries/sdbus-cpp)
  * md4c        - Markdown C parser (from the SBo repo)

Optional at runtime (no build impact): upower, power-profiles-daemon,
ddcutil, libheif (dlopen'd for HEIC/HEIF/AVIF), a Secret Service provider
(GNOME Keyring / KWallet), sound-theme-freedesktop, a running PipeWire daemon
+ WirePlumber.

Build options used (in the .SlackBuild)
---------------------------------------
  --prefix=/usr --libdir=lib64 --buildtype=release
  -Djemalloc=enabled         # recommended on glibc
  -Dtests=disabled
  -Dnative_optimizations=false   # portable; do not enable for distro
  -Dsystem_libraries=false         # use vendored Luau/fzy/MCU/Wuffs

Install layout
--------------
  /usr/bin/noctalia
  /usr/libexec/noctalia/noctalia-pam-helper   (lock screen auth)
  /usr/share/noctalia/assets/                 (REQUIRED at runtime)
  /usr/share/applications/dev.noctalia.*.desktop
  /usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/noctalia.svg
  /usr/share/{bash-completion,zsh,fish} completions (generated)

Source + checksum
-----------------
  https://github.com/noctalia-dev/noctalia/releases/download/v5.5.0/noctalia-v5.5.0.tar.gz
  MD5SUM   424a8e2aa77ffdac693425e284e61b9f
  SHA256   a4ba61392de6024905513d6b070cf40839809f61953468bda7eb8272f7a7aa16

The archive extracts to a top-level `noctalia-release/` dir; the SlackBuild
strips it to `noctalia-5.5.0/`. Download into the build dir and name it
noctalia-5.5.0.tar.gz, then run ./noctalia.SlackBuild.

Notes
-----
* Shell completions are not shipped upstream; they are generated from the
  freshly built binary during install (optional, non-fatal).
* The built prefix / datadir are compiled into the binary, so the package
  must be installed at /usr (do not relocate the prefix after configure).
